<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Resources the shrinker must not remove.

  A release build runs R8 and the resource shrinker, which keep only what they
  can see referenced from code or from another resource. Everything listed here
  is named to Android as a *string*, from Dart, which the shrinker cannot follow.

  `ic_notification` is Musync's own: the small icon handed to
  `JustAudioBackground.init`.

  `audio_service_*` are the seven media-control icons that ship inside the
  audio_service package, referenced from `MediaControl.androidIcon` — strings
  like 'drawable/audio_service_play_arrow'. All seven were being deleted, and
  that is what kept the media notification from ever appearing:

    W System.err: java.lang.IllegalArgumentException:
      You must specify an icon resource id to build a CustomAction

  `AudioService.getResourceId` resolved each name to 0, building the playback
  state's actions threw, and `enterPlayingState()` never reached
  `startForeground`. So no notification, no lock-screen controls, and no
  notification channel was ever even created — while the audio itself played
  perfectly, because just_audio does not go through any of this. Nothing was
  logged on the Dart side, because the throw was on the Java one.

  Release builds only, which is why it survived every test and every debug run.

  Anything else Musync ever names from Dart rather than from code belongs here
  too.
-->
<resources
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@drawable/ic_notification,@drawable/audio_service_*" />
